From ce64f8f904243d6efed1365a7201f786757fa0b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Junod <donujp@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 02:21:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] edid: expose structured extension parsing failures

The global diagnostic string mixes descriptive base-block warnings with
extension ambiguity. Rejecting that entire string hides valid native
DisplayID data on panels with unrelated base timing or range warnings.

Track known extension failures independently of logger formatting. Include
extension diagnostics, discarded/uninterpretable extension records, checksum
failures before early drops, and all input-size/block-count mismatches.
Preserve fatal base header/version/checksum checks. Base descriptive warnings
remain visible without setting extension status. The additive query reports
known failures, not full conformance, opaque-field validation or readiness.

Public-API regressions cover unrelated base warnings, ordinary/nested
extension failures, silent unsupported-version drops, inner/outer checksums,
revision-conditioned unknown tags, known opaque extensions, all framing
mismatches and fatal base checks. GCC analysis and Clang address/undefined
sanitizer suites pass all 75 tests.
---
 edid.c                         |  31 +++++-
 include/edid.h                 |   1 +
 include/libdisplay-info/edid.h |  14 +++
 include/log.h                  |   1 +
 log.c                          |   1 +
 test/edid-extension-failures.c | 198 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 test/meson.build               |   4 +
 test/native-api-consumer.c     |   1 +
 8 files changed, 246 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)
